📄 PaisaVasool Auth Service — Test Documentation


1. Overview

This document defines test cases for the Auth Service, covering:

Health endpoints
Authentication flows
Admin operations
Validation rules

Each test validates input, behavior, and expected responses.

2. Health Check Endpoints
2.1 GET /health

Liveness check — verifies the service is running.

Field	Value
Method	GET
URL	/health
Auth Required	No
Expected Status	200 OK
Expected Response	{ "status": "ok" }
2.2 GET /health/ready

Readiness check — verifies database connectivity.

Scenario	Expected Status	Expected Response
DB connected	200 OK	{ "status": "ok", "checks": { "postgres": "ok" } }
DB unreachable	200 OK	{ "status": "degraded", "checks": { "postgres": "error" } }
3. Authentication Endpoints
3.1 POST /register

Registers a new user.

Scenario	Input	Expected Status	Expected Response
Valid registration	Valid email, phone, password	200	{ "message": "User registered successfully" }
Email already exists	Duplicate email	400	{ "detail": "Email already exists" }
Phone already exists	Duplicate phone	400	{ "detail": "Phone number already exists" }
Invalid phone	Incorrect format	422	Validation error
Weak password	Missing rules	422	Validation error
3.2 POST /login

Authenticates user and returns access token.

Scenario	Input	Expected Status	Expected Response
Valid credentials	Email + password	200	access_token, user_id, email, role
User not found	Invalid email	401	{ "detail": "Invalid credentials" }
Wrong password	Incorrect password	401	{ "detail": "Invalid credentials" }
Missing fields	Empty input	422	Validation error
3.3 GET /auth/me

Returns authenticated user details.

Scenario	Expected Status	Expected Response
Valid token	200	{ "user_id": ..., "email": ..., "role": ... }
No token	401/403	Unauthorized
Expired token	401/403	Unauthorized
3.4 POST /logout

Logs out user by invalidating session.

Scenario	Expected Status	Expected Response
Valid session	200	{ "message": "Logged out successfully" }
No cookie	401	{ "detail": "Already logged out or session expired." }
Invalid cookie	403	{ "detail": "Invalid session" }
3.5 POST /refresh

Generates new access token using refresh token.

Scenario	Expected Status	Expected Response
Valid token	200	{ "access_token": ..., "token_type": "bearer" }
No cookie	403	{ "detail": "Session expired" }
Revoked token	403	{ "detail": "Session revoked" }
Invalid token	403	{ "detail": "Invalid session" }
4. Admin Endpoints
4.1 GET /admin/users

Fetch all non-admin users.

Scenario	Expected Status	Expected Response
Admin access	200	List of users
Non-admin	403	Forbidden
No token	401	Unauthorized
4.2 POST /admin/users

Create new user (admin only).

Scenario	Expected Status	Expected Response
Valid request	200	User object
Duplicate email	400	{ "detail": "Email exists" }
Duplicate phone	400	{ "detail": "Phone exists" }
Non-admin	403	Forbidden
4.3 PATCH /admin/users/{user_id}/toggle-status

Toggle user active/inactive status.

Scenario	Expected Status	Expected Response
Valid request	200	Updated user
User not found	404	{ "detail": "User not found" }
Non-admin	403	Forbidden
5. Validation Rules
5.1 Password Rules
Rule	Example Fail
Minimum 6 characters	abc
At least one lowercase	ABC123!
At least one uppercase	abc123!
At least one number	Abcdef!
At least one special char	Abcdef1
5.2 Phone Number Rules
Input	Valid
9080014226	Yes
1234567890	No
90800	No
90800142261	No
6. Notes
Authentication required endpoints must include Bearer token
Refresh token is stored in HttpOnly cookie
Admin endpoints require role = admin
/seed-admin must be executed before admin tests
/health/ready depends on database availability
